<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Mutawakkil Isma'il</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1676</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Mutawakkil Isma'il was the Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> from 1644 to 1676 and the most powerful ruler of the Qasimid state. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasim-ibn-muhammad">al-Mansur al-Qasim</a>, founder of the dynasty, he extended Zaydi rule over Lower Yemen and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, Lahej and Hadramawt, uniting most of the country after the Ottoman withdrawal. He was also known as a scholar of Zaydi law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-mutawakkil-ismail.jpg" alt="Al-Mutawakkil Isma'il" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tiwahi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zaydi_State_1675.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
